# HTSA close pages — the short enrollment instrument

## Relationship to the older rule

`.cursor/rules/htsa-enrollment-invoice-workflow.mdc` covers the **legacy long
enrollment page** (`htsa-enrollment-*.html`, ~10,000px, locked pay zone).
**This rule takes priority for anything CJ asks for as a "close page".**
Do not merge the two templates. Do not port sections from the legacy page into
this one. Do not modify existing legacy pages when building a new close page.

## Trigger

CJ says **"close page"**, **"enrollment link"**, or **"close link"** and pastes some or all of:
name, email, phone, track, offer, which payment options to show.

Do everything below without follow-up questions. Use the fallbacks and say what you assumed.

## What this page is for

CJ is **on the phone or Zoom with them right now**. They have already verbally
agreed to a plan. This page confirms a decision that was already made. It is not
a brochure and it is not for reading alone. Every extra word on it costs money.

Target: under 3,500px on a 390px viewport. If a change pushes it past that, cut something.

## Never hand-rebuild

```
SOURCE:  templates/_TEMPLATE-close.html
OUTPUT:  htsa-enrollment-<first>-<last>.html      (repo root, matches existing convention)
```

Live URL becomes `https://closewithcjclay.com/htsa-enrollment-<first>-<last>.html`

Never write one from scratch. Never "improve" the template's layout, CSS, copy,
guarantee wording, or tracking while making someone's page.

## Step 1 — copy, then edit ONLY the BUYER block

```js
const BUYER = {
  firstName: "Test",
  fullName:  "Test Person",
  email:     "test@example.com",
  phone:     "+15555550100",              // E.164
  slug:      "test_person",               // must match the filename
  track:     "closer",                    // "closer" or "setter"
  offer:     "standard",                  // "standard" or "reactivation"
  show:      ["pif", "plan", "clarity"]   // which options appear, in this order
};
```

`slug` drives the rows in CJ's Google Sheet. If it does not match the filename his
tracking breaks silently. Check it.

`show` is how CJ controls what is offered. If he says "PIF and ClarityPay only",
set `show: ["pif","clarity"]` and the 4-pay card is removed from the DOM entirely.

## Step 2 — the offer modes

Never edit prices inline. Set `offer` and the whole set swaps.

| | standard | reactivation |
|---|---|---|
| PIF | $6,000 | $5,000 |
| Plan | 4 × $1,750 = $7,000 | 3 × $1,750 = $5,250 |
| ClarityPay | $600/mo · $7,200 total | $500/mo · $6,000 total |

## Step 3 — a negotiated one-off price

If CJ says he agreed a custom number on the call, uncomment `CUSTOM_OFFER` and fill it.
It renders as a navy card **above** every other option and removes the "best value"
badge from PIF.

Never put a negotiated price in a paragraph without a working button. The legacy
page did that and the best offer became the only one the person could not buy.

## Step 4 — promotion / reactivation checkouts (saved)

Canonical table: `templates/HTSA-SECONDARY-PAYMENT-OPTIONS.md` (Promotion / reactivation).
Wired into `OFFERS.reactivation` in `templates/_TEMPLATE-close.html`.

| Offer | Total | Checkout |
|---|---|---|
| PIF | $5,000 | `https://whop.com/checkout/plan_gdThsrGLXqaDF?d2c=true` |
| 3-Pay $1,750 | $5,250 | `https://whop.com/checkout/plan_YrqGOXMxGbOVa?d2c=true` |
| $6k ClarityPay | $6,000 ($500/mo × 12) | `https://whop.com/checkout/plan_VUSDju20gTBCg/` |

Do **not** use the standard 4-pay (`plan_m6yk0QLbxWaak`) for the 3-pay promo.
Do **not** use the standard Closer ClarityPay (`…/1ba2LjGOo3B1Wpp4jf-eF61-w5X4-yCzD-25zhqI3VcVLf/`, $600/mo · $7,200) for the $6k promo.

Any `[PLACEHOLDER]` checkout is caught at click time and alerts instead of charging.
Keep that guard.

## Step 5 — do not move these

- **Terms + curriculum links stay at the bottom**, below the next-steps dropdown. CJ
  explicitly does not want them near the top.
- **Next steps is a collapsed `<details>` directly under the payment buttons.**
  Summary: "Doing this on your own? Here's exactly what happens next". Closed by
  default, always openable, never gated on payment. First open fires
  `next_steps_opened`. Do not hide this section until checkout.
- **Terms acceptance happens after plan selection**, inside the confirm sheet. Never
  gate the payment buttons behind a terms checkbox again. That is what killed
  conversion on the legacy page.
- **The guarantee stays navy and green.** No gold, no brown, no yellow.
- **No curriculum content on the page itself.** Outcomes in the "What you're getting"
  list, detail behind the modal. A visible module list invites evaluation at the
  moment CJ needs a decision.

## Step 6 — verify before reporting done

1. Page height under 3,500px at 390px width.
2. No horizontal scroll at 320px and 375px. No console errors.
3. No rendered text under 12px.
4. Header shows Prepared for (their name/email/phone) and Prepared by (CJ).
5. Only the options in `show` are present, in that order.
6. Footer business card renders with the headshot.
7. Tapping a plan opens the confirm sheet. Continue stays disabled until the box is
   checked. On continue, `recordTermsAgreement` fires before the redirect.
8. In reactivation mode: 3-pay goes to `plan_YrqGOXMxGbOVa` (true 3-pay, no
   fourth-payment warning). ClarityPay goes to `plan_VUSDju20gTBCg` ($6k), not
   the $7,200 closer plan.
9. Next steps is a closed `<details>` under the payment buttons. Opening it
   fires `next_steps_opened` once. It is never hidden behind checkout.

## Step 7 — ship it

```bash
cd ~/Desktop/closewithcjclay.com/closewithcjclay.com
git add htsa-enrollment-<first>-<last>.html
git commit -m "Add close page for <Full Name>"
git push
```

Give CJ the live URL and tell him to load it once himself before the call.

## Step 8 — output the send-it text

Print this ready to copy. **Follow `no-dashes-in-client-copy.mdc`: no em dashes,
no en dashes.** Never write a negative descriptive norm about other prospects.

```
[Message 1]
Here you go, <First>. Everything we just went over is on this page.

[Message 2]
https://closewithcjclay.com/htsa-enrollment-<first>-<last>.html
```

Then remind CJ of the live close process:

```
1. Get the verbal on WHICH plan before sending anything.
2. Say "I'm texting you a page right now, stay on with me, takes about 90 seconds."
3. Send it while you are still talking. Never send and hang up.
4. Narrate it: "Top green box says Paid in Full. Tap it."
5. Terms sheet is one line: "That's the terms and the guarantee, check the box, hit continue."
6. Stay on the line through Whop. Do not go quiet. Talk about their start date.
7. They text "payment confirmed", you turn on access while still on the phone.
```
